# Plan: opt-in OpenAI fixed-greeting interruption

## Goal

Add experimental `greetingInterruption?: false | true | BrowserVadOptions` support to `OpenAIAdapter`. While a fixed greeting is active, the first locally accepted speech boundary must stop local greeting playback, then flush one bounded `LocalAudioPreRoll` tail, then pass live microphone audio. Explicit **Skip greeting** remains the reliable control.

Omitted and `false` configuration must preserve the existing raw-track runtime and initial bundle path. Enabled configuration must validate synchronously. VAD or AudioWorklet failure must safely return to the existing non-interruptible greeting gate without publishing greeting-period audio or failing an otherwise healthy voice session. `GreetingPresentation` composes a package-private interruption owner. `OpenAIAdapter` only prepares and attaches the selected publication track and performs generation-fenced sender replacement when the owner requests recovery.

Normal OpenAI turn ownership remains unchanged after greeting settlement. Preserve at-most-once Engine/provider greeting history, immediate and transcript-confirmed behavior, response arbitration, turn mode, bounded diagnostics, exact cleanup, reconnect isolation, and raw-stream metering.

